      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s spelling dropped the “h” in patriotic protest after the Townshend Acts of 1767, becoming “Townsend” by 1780.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
